  "published": "2026-07-08",
  "insights": [
   "Shopify is updating its partner model effective August 10, 2026, to better align partner economics with merchant growth and incentivize upmarket expansion.",
   "The new model offers partners 20% revenue share on subscription fees and 0.1% of eligible online GMV for four years, replacing the previous perpetual 20% subscription revenue share.",
   "Additional incentives include a $2,500 one-time bonus for Plus upgrades, extended POS Payments profit share (from 2 to 4 years), and new B2B payments profit share.",
   "The bank views the changes as a modest positive, expecting them to strengthen the ecosystem and drive market share gains in complex implementations (Plus, POS, B2B).",
   "Potential risks include the impact of the 4-year term limit and whether it disincentivizes partners from working with smaller merchants that require longer-term growth."
